---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Case Study: The Self-Driving PSUR — Medivora"
  description="How top pharmaceutical companies use Generative AI to automate Periodic Safety Update Reports (PSUR)."
>
  <article class="case-study-page">
    <header class="cs-hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <a href="/case-studies" class="back-link">← All Case Studies</a>
        <div class="cs-meta">
          <span class="cs-pill">Aggregate</span>
          <span class="cs-org">Top 20 Pharma</span>
        </div>
        <h1>Automated PSUR / PBRER Drafting</h1>
        <p class="cs-lede">Transforming Medical Writers into Medical Editors by using Generative AI to synthesize thousands of line listings into submission-ready aggregate reports.</p>

        <div class="cinematic-image-wrapper">
          <img src="/images/pv_cs_psur.png" alt="Glowing medical aggregate report document" class="cinematic-img">
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="wrap cs-content">
      <div class="cs-main">
        <h2>The Challenge</h2>
        <p>
          Drafting Periodic Safety Update Reports (PSURs) and Periodic Benefit-Risk Evaluation Reports (PBRERs) is an incredibly labor-intensive process. A single report can take a team of medical writers weeks to complete. They must extract data from the safety database, compile complex summary tabulations, and manually write narrative summaries describing patient exposure and safety signals over the reporting interval.
        </p>

        <h2>The Automation Solution</h2>
        <p>
          A Top 20 Pharma company implemented a "Medical Writing Copilot" to automate the creation of the first draft of these reports.
        </p>
        <p>
          The architecture separates deterministic data gathering from generative drafting:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Data Extraction:</strong> A SQL-based agent queries the safety database to generate the mandatory summary tabulations (e.g., interval vs. cumulative AE counts) with 100% mathematical accuracy.</li>
          <li><strong>Generative Drafting:</strong> A long-context LLM ingests the previous year's PSUR (for stylistic consistency and context), the new summary tabulations, and the Risk Management Plan (RMP). It then drafts the narrative sections, such as the presentation of safety data and interval analysis.</li>
          <li><strong>Traceability:</strong> The AI inserts hyperlinked citations for every numerical claim, allowing the medical writer to click a number and immediately see the underlying line listing that generated it.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>The Outcomes</h2>
        <p>
          The implementation drastically reduced the time spent on document creation. Medical writers transitioned from manual data gatherers to high-level reviewers and editors. The "first draft" generation time dropped from weeks to hours, achieving a 60% overall reduction in the end-to-end aggregate reporting lifecycle, while simultaneously reducing copy-paste errors to zero.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="cs-sidebar">
        <div class="metrics-card">
          <h4>Key Results</h4>
          <div class="metric">
            <span class="m-val">60%</span>
            <span class="m-lbl">Faster end-to-end reporting</span>
          </div>
          <div class="metric">
            <span class="m-val">Zero</span>
            <span class="m-lbl">Copy-paste data errors</span>
          </div>
          <div class="metric">
            <span class="m-val">100%</span>
            <span class="m-lbl">Data lineage traceability</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sources-card">
          <h4>References &amp; Standards</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <a href="https://database.ich.org/sites/default/files/E2C_R2_Guideline.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ICH E2C (R2) Guideline on PBRER</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span>Generative AI in Medical Writing Consortiums</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span>Enterprise safety software case studies (e.g., ArisG / Veeva)</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Same CSS as literature-intake.astro */
  .case-study-page { background: var(--color-bg); padding-bottom: 5rem; }
  .cs-hero { background: var(--color-surface); padding: 4rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line); margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .back-link { display: inline-block; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--color-text-soft); text-decoration: none; margin-bottom: 2rem; transition: color 200ms ease; }
  .back-link:hover { color: var(--color-accent); }
  .cs-meta { display: flex; gap: 1rem; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .cs-pill { background: rgba(28,201,163,0.1); color: #1cc9a3; padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: 100px; font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; font-family: var(--font-mono); }
  .cs-org { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--color-text-soft); letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
  .cs-hero h1 { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem); line-height: 1.2; color: var(--color-text); margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .cs-lede { font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--color-text-2); max-width: 45em; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 2rem; }

  /* ── Cinematic Images ── */
  .cinematic-image-wrapper {
    margin: 0 auto 3rem;
    max-width: 100%;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid rgba(241, 236, 224, 0.1);
    box-shadow: 0 20px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
  }
  .cinematic-img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 21 / 9;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center 50%;
    display: block;
    transition: transform 0.8s ease;
  }
  .cinematic-image-wrapper:hover .cinematic-img {
    transform: scale(1.02);
  }

  .cs-content { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr; gap: 4rem; }
  @media (max-width: 800px) { .cs-content { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 3rem; } }
  .cs-main h2 { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 1.8rem; color: var(--color-text); margin-top: 2.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .cs-main h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .cs-main p { font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-text-2); margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .cs-main ul { font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-text-2); margin-bottom: 1.5rem; padding-left: 1.5rem; }
  .cs-main li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .cs-main strong { color: var(--color-text); }
  .metrics-card, .sources-card { background: var(--color-surface); border: 1px solid var(--color-line); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .metrics-card h4, .sources-card h4 { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.85rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: var(--color-text); margin-bottom: 1.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line); padding-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .metric { margin-bottom: 1.2rem; }
  .metric:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .m-val { display: block; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 1.8rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1cc9a3; line-height: 1.2; }
  .m-lbl { display: block; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--color-text-soft); }
  .sources-card ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  .sources-card li { margin-bottom: 1rem; font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .sources-card li:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .sources-card a { color: var(--color-accent); text-decoration: none; transition: color 200ms ease; }
  .sources-card a:hover { color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-accent) 80%, white); text-decoration: underline; }
  .sources-card span { color: var(--color-text-2); }
</style>
